WEBVTT

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.190
Shut up, bitch!

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.390
Satsuki!

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.790
Unbelievable...

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.840
She doesn't know anything!

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.660
That old hag!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.150
Stupid bitch!

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.350
Old hag...

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.100
Ugh, dammit!

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.920
What do you want?

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.090
That was a good shot.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.350
Sure, just take it without asking.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.500
Sorry...

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.080
The photographer in me just can't
resist when I see a good subject.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.820
You're creeping me out, old man.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.990
Well, that hurts...

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.460
I thought I'd still be considered a young guy.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.930
You wanna buy me?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.800
I wanna save up to run away.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.280
I'll pass.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:48.040
I'm not quite bold enough to get involved 
with a girl wearing a training bra.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:15.340
Hanasaku Iroha

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:34.880
Kissuiso

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.040
So how much?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.950
Make it cheap.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.190
Well, let's see...

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.160
How about a single silver coin?

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.290
I think that's pretty reasonable.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.620
What? 100 yen?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.330
That's too much, old man!

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.780
Is it? I <i>am</i> a professional, after all.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.100
And plus...

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.610
It starts to get better after here...

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.980
Eh!? Ohana? You mean that shorty?

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.050
I don't want it, if she's the main character.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:25.860
Right?

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:26.900
What?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.330
You should know, Ohana-chan is
of an especially good quality.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:35.100
The more you chew, 
the more flavor you'll get...

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.430
I appreciate the compliment.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.790
Crap, it's Ohana!

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.260
I can't handle the real deal!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.220
Same here!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.380
The real deal, eh...?

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:51.190
How can you interrupt my
business like this, Ohana-chan?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:55.880
Isn't this—!?

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.370
<i>The Hot Spring Attendant and Her 
Bubbly</i>-thingy from some time ago!?

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.300
I took the time to complete it,
so I figured I'd at least rent it out.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:05.980
Rent it out!?

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.400
Indeed!

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:12.260
Delivering my work to those who
understand and appreciate it...

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.870
You know, renting books has 
quite a storied history...

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.740
It all began with that famous—

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.540
I'm sorry!

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.660
Jeez, I can't believe he
kept writing this thing...

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.960
"I-I want to sparkle!"
"Don't worry. If we scrub you right here..."

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.420
I want to sparkle!

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.520
"Sparkle"...huh?

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.130
All right! Gotta work, gotta work!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.620
I understand. Thank you for your hard work.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.240
It's just some routine maintenance, 
so it'll only take about three hours.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:17.270
Please finish it as quickly as possible
to avoid inconveniencing our guests.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.030
The ability to generate electricity
from wasted enthusiasm...

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:27.320
I wonder if such a technology can 
be invented while I'm still alive.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.310
<i>The routine of Kissuiso has 
become my "normal" life.</i>

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.970
<i>I think I've pretty much 
gotten used to work...</i>

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.560
<i>But...</i>

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:57.230
I'll admit I've kinda started to forget
about the desire I had to sparkle...

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:07.290
I know I polished this area a lot, 
so it looks pretty sparkly to me...

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.260
What's this?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.310
It looks like a person's face...

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.910
Shall I polish your forehead?

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.060
Squeaky, squeaky clean...

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.620
But just polishing here won't—

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:33.700
Aww, a step? So not fair!

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.980
Yuina-san!?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.460
Oh, so sorry, ya know?

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.790
Ren-san, should we use this all up, too?

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.700
Yeah. Food's quick to spoil.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.990
Make sure you cook all the perishables.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:50.740
Yes, sir.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.570
Make sweet simmered fish with this one.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.200
The pork shoulder's thawed, 
so just cube and stew that.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.690
Use more soy sauce, and—

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:58.810
There you all are!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.440
Heeeeeeey!

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.500
Yuina-san...

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.180
It's Tohru-san and Tsurugi-san!

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.800
You shouldn't distract them.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.930
Oh hey, who was the guy 
with the crew cut again?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.580
You... How could you—!?

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.150
Eww, it's still alive! So gross!

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:23.050
Oh look, if you decorate 
this with some dandelions...

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.000
- Yui— 
- El completo!

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.690
Ta-da!

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.470
Oh sashimi, so purty!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.520
- Whatcha think!? 
- Huh? Uh, um...

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.750
Get out...

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.080
G-G—

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.420
GET OUT!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.940
Yuina-san!

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:45.790
I'm training to be a Madam Manager.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.210
I need to learn all kinds of stuff!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.120
Jeez.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.610
Training...at Kissuiso?

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.430
Yep!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.270
Just temporarily for the 
fall's holiday season.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.160
It was a request from 
Fukuya's Madam Manager.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.090
She wants Yuina to familiarize herself 
with the methods of the other inns.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:06.150
Methods...right.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.840
I'm still inexperienced, so I'd
appreciate it if you looked after me.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.340
M-Madam Manag—

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.490
Well, I'm leaving this to you now.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.620
Huh? M-Me?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.100
Why? M-Madam Manager?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.860
It's all you now, Ohana-chan!

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.780
S-Sure...

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:32.260
For some reason, I feel like a huge 
 burden got dumped on me...

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.580
Don't worry, Ohana-chan!

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.460
Th-Thanks...

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.040
- Now then! Shall we get started!? 
- Ah, Yuina-san... Wait!

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.150
<i>Regarding last week's 
typhoon on the east coa—</i>

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:45.820
All right...

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.350
Let's start the meeting.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:51.410
We mentioned the power outage 
during the reservation process,

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:54.930
but make sure to remind the guests when
you serve the welcome tea and sweets.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:58.030
The bath times for men and women 
have changed, as well—

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.140
Okay, so when serving tea and sweets...

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:04.330
Since it's just a few hours in the day, 
I'm sure we'll get through it somehow.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.240
I'm sure the guests will be out
looking around the area—

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.170
No, no!

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:12.530
"Somehow"? We must always 
prioritize our guests!

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:18.860
The same way you would treat 
your fiancé. Nice and SWEET.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.940
Like my fiancé?

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:21.740
Exactly.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.290
"I'm all yours."

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.680
"If it's for your sake..."

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.590
"I would go through fire...through water..."

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.570
Right, Takako?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:39.610
It might be tough for you to understand, 
since you don't have anyone in your life.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:44.720
But singles can use their abundant 
imagination to compensate for that.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.000
T-Tomoe-san...

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.180
What was up with that stupid show!?

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.540
- Dammit! I'm fed up! Those dumbasses! 
- T-Tomoe-san!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:57.130
Well, damn right, I don't understand it!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.760
So what if I've never experienced it before!?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.400
U-Um...

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:01.300
I don't care!

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:05.850
I have a job that I love! 
Who cares about fiancés!?

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.220
Dagnabbit!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.580
Argh, I can't get it right!

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:18.540
It just gets more wrinkly!

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.980
Um, that's not true. C'mon.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.690
Like you're stretching it out...

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:34.460
Go on, hold down the corner here.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.970
Huh? O-Okay...

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:39.180
Now slide your hand across like this...

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:40.300
Slide.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.590
I did it!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.530
Yep. Great job.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:49.990
Amazing! You're such a
good teacher, Tomoe-san!

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:52.150
Oh yeah?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:56.840
Your kids are so lucky to 
have a nice mom like you.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.790
Huh? Kids?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:05.280
I figured that you must be a mom
because of how mature you are.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.540
Was I wrong?

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.790
A mom or whatever...

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.340
I haven't even taken the first
step toward making babies!

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.050
NOT EVEN THE FIRST STEP!

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:17.710
Jeez... You need to be careful...

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.760
Tomoe-san is sensitive about that topic.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.360
All right...

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:27.230
Okay Yuina-san, could you store 
all the old yukata over he—

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.100
Oh, shoot...

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:31.690
The sheets are almost done washing.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.050
Oh, go ahead.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.900
I can put away the yukata all by myself.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.440
Huh? But...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.990
Ain't nuthin' to worry 'bout!

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:41.990
You're sure?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:45.070
Then I'll just finish wiping 
the floors while I'm at it.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.340
G'luck to ya!

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.370
Okay, then...

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:56.940
Despite what I said, this work is 
seriously tedious and boring.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.690
I wanna work on something more exciting...

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.410
Oh sorry, Nakochi.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.580
It's no problem.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.580
You seem tired, Nakochi.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.920
Yeah, a little.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.580
My mom and dad are both 
away on a training trip.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.860
They're both teachers, right?

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:50.680
That must be tough. Are you 
doing all the chores yourself?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.420
Yeah, but it's actually not much
more than what I usually do.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.040
But then...

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:04.830
The day after tomorrow, my little 
sister, Mana, is going potato picking...

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.420
Potato picking...

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.330
Yeah, for a field trip...

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.290
At first, my mom was gonna take
the day off to go with her...

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.210
Which made her really happy...

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:16.290
She must be disappointed now...

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.330
I know the feeling!

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:22.240
The higher the expectation,
the bigger the disappointment!

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:26.280
Which always turns into
an unforgettable pain...

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.360
...that lasts for years!

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:34.000
D-Did I just make things worse?

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.600
N-No...

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.920
B-But it's going to be okay!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.920
Because, you know, she'll eventually 
stop caring very much...

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:47.030
She'll stop wishing to have a happy 
household, and learn to live pretty okay!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.580
Even I...

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:53.710
S-Sorry! Was that a sensitive topic for you?

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.350
Ren-san, the simmered dish is finished.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.140
Good.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.400
Hey Tohru, should I change up the crew cut—

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.120
Cold cuts? But I've already
started the cubed pork.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.640
Oh, I see...

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.110
Okay, that's fine...

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.860
Hey Minko, is that done over there?

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.110
Y-Yes, it's ready!

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.370
Let me see.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.580
O-Okay.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.260
Wh-What do you think?

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:47.820
Details for tomorrow's reservations?

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:50.170
Um, well, I think they were...

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:55.550
A family with children, and a couple who
was celebrating an 88th bir—

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:56.470
No good.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.890
Ren-san, I'll take care of the simmered fish.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.810
Sure. Take care to not use too 
much honey while finishing it. {while plating it?}

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:03.500
Yes, sir.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:14.220
<i>Nakochi does such a great job.
She's handling all the chores at home...</i>

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:18.700
<i>And not just that, she also cares 
about her siblings so much...</i>

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:22.570
Nakochi's like a real mom...

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:27.310
<i>An ideal mom at that...</i>

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:31.380
<i>My relationship with my mom was a little...</i>

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.410
<i>I mean, it was super weird...I think.</i>

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:41.360
<i>I used to expect some things when I was 
little, but I eventually gave up on them.</i>

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:47.150
<i>It's not like I hate my mom, but...</i>

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:56.390
<i>Mom doesn't get me...</i>

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:01.190
<i>But on the other hand, 
I don't get her either...</i>

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.590
Oh man! This is too dang fun! 
What do you think, Gramps!?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.880
- Um, can you...
- Snippity, snip!

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.500
- I think we should switch now...
- It needs more originality!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.510
A heart-shaped bonsai would be cute!

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.170
- Well, that...
- Snip, snip!

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.520
- ...may be a bad idea...
- Snippity, snip, snip!

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.980
Did Yuina-san even finish with the storage?

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:36.060
S-Such a terrible mess!

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.710
What is this? Jeez!

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.000
Seriously...

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:41.830
Logbook

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.470
Is this Beans's log...?

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:54.950
"About thirty percent of the 
garden turns to fall colors."

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:57.530
"The Miyoshi couple comes to the inn."

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.250
"Today's meal is pork soup
 and sea veggie rice."

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.670
He even records that stuff, huh?

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.980
"'I want to sparkle,'"

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:11.450
"said Satsuki-chan."

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:19.000
Madam Manager, it seems the guests in 
the Camellia Room are arriving late.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.460
Understood.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.460
Yunosagi Bonbori
Festival 1989

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:22.880
Aki-san, did you finish 
cleaning the Wave Room?

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:23.780
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:28.380
Madam Manager, the guests in the Crane 
Room asked about tomorrow's breakfast.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.610
I'll be there right away.

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:33.080
Mom, um, I want a snack...

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.700
Have Satsuki get it for you!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.510
B-But...

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:39.730
Enishi?

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.810
Where are you going?

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.740
To a study group with my friends.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:48.260
Who's going to take care of Enishi?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.140
I have to study for exams. I don't
 have time to babysit him.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.070
Satsuki!

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.800
Please don't fight!

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.580
I don't want a snack anymore.

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:29.110
Madam Manager!

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.700
I'm all right. I just felt a little lightheaded.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.690
Please don't overwork yourself.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:37.240
Your lights were on late last night again...

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:41.960
That means you were up 
late working, too, right?

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.790
"Kissuiso isn't the same after the owner died."

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.030
"Their Madam Manager can't
manage it after all."

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.240
I won't give people a chance
 to say those things.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.000
That's why...

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:00.450
Gain the Strength to Survive
 an Internationalized Society

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.440
You're a criminal.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.910
Taking pictures without permission.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.660
Yunosagi really is a wonderful place.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:24.930
Nature is left untouched, and its
girls are in their natural state.

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:26.780
I can't help but take photos.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.930
Are you calling me a bumpkin!?

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:34.220
Only out here could you find a young 
girl using the word "bumpkin."

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.880
Hey, wait...

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:50.050
You want to go to a college in Tokyo?

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:03.820
Not Tokyo specifically...

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:08.010
I just want to go as far away 
as possible from that place.

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.040
That place?

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:14.110
I feel like I'm going to rot
away if I stay there.

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:17.460
I want...to sparkle more.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.660
You're already glistening enough, though.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:38.290
The next train isn't for thirty minutes...

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:50.290
What's the deal with that guy? Is he hot?

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:51.320
Not really...

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:53.380
He's kind of scrawny.

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:55.800
Hey, you better be savoring that.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.630
It's what you get for being late.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.890
Heya, are you really going to buy 
something <i>that</i> scandalous?

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:04.290
5,000 yen!?

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:05.700
I don't have enough... Spot me!

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:06.890
No way!

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.050
Satsuki-chan!

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:16.420
Didn't you go to study? 
So what is this?

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:18.420
Give it back!

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:21.420
I used my own allowance 
so it's totally fine!

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:24.010
And where do you think 
that allowance comes from!?

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:27.510
Buying such risqué undergarments...

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:28.330
How shameful!

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:31.220
Girls in Tokyo wear things like this!

00:22:31.220 --> 00:22:33.540
And I'm going to go to Tokyo, too!

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:37.110
And what do you intend to
do once you reach Tokyo?

00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:42.390
You don't even have your 
own goal or dream.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.430
But Tokyo this, Tokyo that...

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:45.850
Life isn't that easy!

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:48.180
I want to sparkle!

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:49.140
Huh...?

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:50.810
But...

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:53.180
But I can't sparkle here...

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:56.080
I don't want to become like you, Mom!

00:22:57.300 --> 00:22:59.660
Clinging to how things used to be,

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:02.490
clinging to Dad's ghost...

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:04.700
You're so caught up in all that...

00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:05.890
It's so stupid!

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:14.850
I'm going to get out of here...

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:18.090
I'll never become like you, Mom...

00:23:18.090 --> 00:23:19.490
Never!

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:20.460
Miss!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:21.510
Satsuki-chan!

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:37.530
"The photographer stays 
at the inn long-term."

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:40.250
"Satsuki-chan gets slapped twice."

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:43.850
It's vague, so I'm not sure, but...

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:51.340
But it seems like Mom also 
once wanted to sparkle...

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:53.600
And on top of that...

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.940
This photographer person...

00:23:56.940 --> 00:23:58.500
He's probably Dad...

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:03.090
<i>The two of them met here.</i>..

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:07.430
<i>And if it means I was born... 
Then that must mean...</i>

00:24:16.870 --> 00:24:19.190
Sorry for not seeing you off.
Do your best, Ohana! —Ko-chan

00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:22.780
<i>See ya.</i>

00:24:28.510 --> 00:24:32.740
That was uber fun! 
See ya tomorrow!

00:24:33.250 --> 00:24:35.220
What's with that girl!?

00:24:35.220 --> 00:24:37.780
Getting in the way of everything...

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.520
Even though it's already chaotic 
enough because of the blackout!

00:24:42.340 --> 00:24:44.780
Oh, want to use this too, Minko?

00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:48.020
Eh? Um...what do you use that for?

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:51.020
Huh? What are you saying?

00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:54.180
You use it to scrape the 
hard calluses off your...

00:24:59.290 --> 00:25:04.600
Ah, my mom's heels get pretty 
rough and yellow, too...

00:25:05.060 --> 00:25:08.230
Thick calluses form when 
you've been working hard!

00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:10.880
You guys don't have enough training yet!

00:25:10.880 --> 00:25:12.450
S-Sorry!

00:25:22.170 --> 00:25:23.750
You've had it rough.

00:25:27.990 --> 00:25:32.230
Nakochi isn't joining us in 
the bath today, is she?

00:25:32.230 --> 00:25:35.140
She's looking after her siblings, right?

00:25:35.140 --> 00:25:37.390
Yeah... It's amazing, isn't it?

00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:39.890
She finishes work, 
then goes to do more.

00:25:39.890 --> 00:25:42.810
Nakochi's having a pretty tough time...

00:25:43.190 --> 00:25:46.370
How should I put it...? 
She acts like a mother.

00:25:47.150 --> 00:25:50.020
I wonder if her heels 
have turned yellow...

00:25:51.870 --> 00:25:52.550
Eh?

00:25:52.550 --> 00:25:53.320
Huh?

00:25:56.250 --> 00:25:58.280
Nako has hiccups!

00:25:56.250 --> 00:25:58.280
Oshimizu Family

00:25:58.280 --> 00:26:00.410
Someone must be talking about you.

00:26:00.410 --> 00:26:03.750
You idiot! That's when you sneeze.

00:26:03.750 --> 00:26:05.460
Oh? Oh!

00:26:06.910 --> 00:26:09.020
Ouch! What was that for?

00:26:09.020 --> 00:26:11.260
I'm scaring you! Boo!

00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:13.190
I'm fine already.

00:26:16.100 --> 00:26:20.030
If you drink water upside down
like this, the hiccups disappear.

00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:21.550
Mana wants to do it too!

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:23.880
Let me try!

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:25.170
Do it! Do it!

00:26:25.820 --> 00:26:26.730
Here you go.

00:26:32.970 --> 00:26:34.600
Ah! Mana!

00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:36.450
She really did it!

00:26:36.450 --> 00:26:38.160
- She spilled everywhere! 
- Jeez...

00:26:38.970 --> 00:26:41.410
Don't make more work for me...

00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:47.910
Oh, that's right!

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:51.740
I was thinking I'd ask for the day 
after tomorrow off, for your field trip.

00:26:52.150 --> 00:26:53.230
Huh?

00:26:53.230 --> 00:26:56.220
So let's go on the field trip together.

00:26:56.220 --> 00:26:57.470
Really!?

00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:01.060
Yay!

00:27:01.450 --> 00:27:02.760
Yay!

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:04.400
- Oh, that's great Mana.
- Yaaay!

00:27:05.770 --> 00:27:09.440
<i>Now, which is the right answer?</i>

00:27:10.830 --> 00:27:15.090
<i>Yes! Uzui-san, from the Rabbit Team! </i>

00:27:12.740 --> 00:27:15.090
We're a little bit over this month...

00:27:15.090 --> 00:27:16.340
<i>A. The tower of Pisa!</i>

00:27:16.340 --> 00:27:19.780
So if we buy a new one, it'd be 
disappointing if she doesn't use it.

00:27:20.430 --> 00:27:22.860
<i>Oh, too bad!</i>

00:27:20.430 --> 00:27:22.860
Nako, read me a story.

00:27:22.860 --> 00:27:25.990
Hmm? Sure, just a minute...

00:27:25.950 --> 00:27:31.140
<i>With Uzui knocked out, 
it's time for the next question.</i>

00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:27.310
Come on, Mana...

00:27:27.310 --> 00:27:30.710
Nako's tired, so let her take a little break.

00:27:30.710 --> 00:27:31.590
Huh?

00:27:31.140 --> 00:27:31.900
<i>Wanna say it?</i>

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:32.830
<i>Want to try it?</i>

00:27:32.830 --> 00:27:33.930
<i>Which one is it?</i>

00:27:33.930 --> 00:27:36.330
<i>But first, a commercial!</i>

00:27:34.040 --> 00:27:36.330
I-It's fine, really.

00:27:38.130 --> 00:27:41.460
"The prince told the princess,"

00:27:41.460 --> 00:27:44.500
"'That's not a bowl. It's a teapot.'"

00:27:57.090 --> 00:27:58.860
Are you awake, Mana?

00:28:09.450 --> 00:28:10.950
Thanks...

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:16.900
Minchi's late tonight.

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:24.930
Glad I grabbed this...

00:28:42.860 --> 00:28:44.140
You're leaving, huh?

00:28:45.500 --> 00:28:48.030
I've already been here a long time.

00:28:49.770 --> 00:28:51.580
And I've gotten lots of good pictures.

00:28:51.950 --> 00:28:54.300
I see. No fair...

00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:58.060
You're coming to Tokyo after 
you graduate, right?

00:29:00.310 --> 00:29:03.700
I said some horrible 
things to my mom.

00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:06.700
That I wanted to get out of this place...

00:29:06.700 --> 00:29:10.500
That, and I even mentioned going to Tokyo.

00:29:10.500 --> 00:29:14.030
But Mom's the one who would 
give me money to go.

00:29:14.200 --> 00:29:16.510
I told her that I want to do
something to sparkle....

00:29:17.810 --> 00:29:20.700
But in the end, I haven't 
thought of anything.

00:29:21.430 --> 00:29:24.460
And even if I went to Tokyo, 
what would I do...?

00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:29.030
Why don't you come to my room?

00:29:30.790 --> 00:29:31.550
Huh?

00:29:35.570 --> 00:29:36.510
What?

00:29:38.220 --> 00:29:39.930
It's a little messy, but...

00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:44.070
Um, actually, I...

00:29:44.070 --> 00:29:45.200
Here.

00:29:51.650 --> 00:29:53.130
No...

00:29:53.620 --> 00:29:56.070
These aren't me...

00:29:56.530 --> 00:30:00.220
I don't sparkle this much...

00:30:00.220 --> 00:30:02.950
This is the Satsuki-chan that I see.

00:30:05.190 --> 00:30:08.590
You just can't see how 
you really shine.

00:30:08.590 --> 00:30:11.570
And no one can shine without 
a goal in their heart.

00:30:12.150 --> 00:30:16.190
You worry a lot, and have a lot of 
conflicts, yet despite all of that...

00:30:16.650 --> 00:30:17.670
Look.

00:30:18.500 --> 00:30:19.920
You're so beautiful.

00:30:27.150 --> 00:30:28.900
Satsuki-chan, what's—

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:31.150
I think I like you!

00:30:31.150 --> 00:30:31.730
Eh?

00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:38.630
I think...

00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:43.140
I think you're confusing your fondness
 for Tokyo with how you feel about me.

00:30:43.140 --> 00:30:44.240
You're acting like an adult!

00:30:44.830 --> 00:30:45.910
You think so...?

00:30:47.610 --> 00:30:49.080
You totally are!

00:31:02.370 --> 00:31:04.690
Aaah, crap!

00:31:08.780 --> 00:31:10.330
Uh...

00:31:15.930 --> 00:31:17.980
Sis!

00:31:17.980 --> 00:31:20.560
Sis, he's leaving!

00:31:20.870 --> 00:31:21.810
Jeez!

00:31:21.810 --> 00:31:22.940
Don't worry, Enishi-kun.

00:31:23.650 --> 00:31:24.590
Here...

00:31:25.890 --> 00:31:27.940
Could you give these to your sister for me?

00:31:28.460 --> 00:31:29.740
She forgot them.

00:31:29.740 --> 00:31:30.620
Okay!

00:31:31.410 --> 00:31:32.480
Thanks.

00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:35.470
Sis!

00:31:39.140 --> 00:31:41.360
I said, Sis!

00:31:41.750 --> 00:31:42.970
Si—

00:32:18.470 --> 00:32:21.890
I'll never say good-bye!

00:32:28.860 --> 00:32:30.860
Okay, I'll let her know.

00:32:30.860 --> 00:32:31.590
The guests in th—

00:32:31.590 --> 00:32:34.220
Madam Manager, it's your daughter's school.

00:32:41.940 --> 00:32:43.980
Satsuki? I'm coming in.

00:32:45.210 --> 00:32:47.650
I just got a call from your school.

00:32:47.890 --> 00:32:50.650
They said you changed which
college you plan to attend.

00:32:50.650 --> 00:32:52.200
Why did you decide behind my back—

00:32:52.200 --> 00:32:53.720
I discovered what I want to do.

00:32:56.580 --> 00:32:59.180
I'm going to become an editor...

00:32:59.850 --> 00:33:02.570
Someday, I want to work with him.

00:33:02.570 --> 00:33:04.220
Him?

00:33:04.220 --> 00:33:08.330
The thing you want to do is 
to chase after some man?

00:33:08.330 --> 00:33:11.410
Isn't that what you did!? 
You chased after Dad!

00:33:11.410 --> 00:33:14.110
- What—? 
- But I won't deny it anymore!

00:33:15.510 --> 00:33:18.510
Please, let me go to Tokyo!

00:33:18.510 --> 00:33:21.270
I'll pay for my living expenses 
by working part-time!

00:33:22.190 --> 00:33:25.960
Please... Let me follow my own dreams!

00:33:32.070 --> 00:33:34.560
"Discovers what she wants to do..."?

00:33:35.180 --> 00:33:37.910
What did Mom discover?

00:33:39.260 --> 00:33:40.340
Huh?

00:33:40.340 --> 00:33:42.490
Why is my heart racing...?

00:33:43.780 --> 00:33:46.260
Huh? What is this?

00:33:47.140 --> 00:33:51.070
Mom was also searching for 
what she wanted to do.

00:33:51.070 --> 00:33:53.640
And it seems she found it...

00:33:55.010 --> 00:33:56.300
<i>It seems obvious, but...</i>

00:33:56.710 --> 00:34:00.230
<i>Ever since I was old enough to know what
was happening, Mom's been very mature.</i>

00:34:00.230 --> 00:34:02.710
<i>But, she's always been a 
pretty messed up adult...</i>

00:34:02.710 --> 00:34:04.810
<i>I couldn't tell what she was thinking.</i>

00:34:04.810 --> 00:34:06.940
<i>And we never really fit together...</i>

00:34:06.940 --> 00:34:10.400
<i>But... She was always very deliberate...</i>

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:17.320
<i>So to think that there was a time...</i>

00:34:17.320 --> 00:34:21.940
<i>...when Mom also wanted to find 
a way to sparkle... Just like me... </i>

00:34:23.700 --> 00:34:25.470
What should I do?

00:34:28.020 --> 00:34:31.530
Man, it's late.

00:34:31.530 --> 00:34:32.540
Huh?

00:34:32.540 --> 00:34:34.310
Crap, my phone.

00:34:38.800 --> 00:34:39.890
Ohana!

00:34:40.430 --> 00:34:42.310
Oh, Tohru-san!

00:34:42.750 --> 00:34:45.150
What are you doing at this hour!?

00:34:45.150 --> 00:34:46.660
Running!

00:34:46.660 --> 00:34:48.490
Well I can see that!

00:34:48.490 --> 00:34:50.830
I guess I got a little excited!

00:34:50.830 --> 00:34:52.350
E-Excited!?

00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:54.620
Yeah! Anyway, I'll see you later!

00:34:54.620 --> 00:34:56.110
Ah, hey...

00:34:59.540 --> 00:35:01.990
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:35:02.280 --> 00:35:04.500
<i>I thought you were an adult
 who couldn't relate.</i>

00:35:04.500 --> 00:35:09.170
<i>But in the past, did you also 
worry, get lost, and fall in love?</i>

00:35:14.930 --> 00:35:16.440
Fall in love?

00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:20.430
<i>Mom...found love.</i>

00:35:22.450 --> 00:35:25.660
<i>I guess...I found someone, too.</i>

00:35:26.510 --> 00:35:28.280
<i>Or I should have...</i>

00:35:38.090 --> 00:35:39.810
What's wrong, Ohana?

00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:43.520
They're from the other class.

00:35:43.520 --> 00:35:44.080
Oh yeah...

00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:47.190
It's not like we're a couple or anything.

00:35:47.190 --> 00:35:50.250
I mean, you don't want
 people to think that, right?

00:35:51.690 --> 00:35:52.690
Ko-chan?

00:35:52.690 --> 00:35:53.670
Well...

00:35:54.380 --> 00:35:56.350
Oh, there's a spot over there.

00:35:56.580 --> 00:36:00.350
Ah, and it's right under a cherry tree!

00:36:01.370 --> 00:36:04.230
<i>Even so, I...</i>

00:36:15.250 --> 00:36:17.790
No good... It's not right.

00:36:21.900 --> 00:36:24.950
<i>I want to be able to make food 
that Tohru-san will approve of.</i>

00:36:25.660 --> 00:36:26.650
<i>But...</i>

00:36:38.580 --> 00:36:41.740
Simmered clam, so purty!

00:36:50.710 --> 00:36:54.910
I never knew girls got that excited 
in the middle of the night....

00:36:55.410 --> 00:36:56.860
I'm going home.

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:22.020
Ah, good morning.

00:37:25.210 --> 00:37:26.850
Y-Yo.

00:37:27.050 --> 00:37:30.700
Re— R-R-R-Ren-san... What 
happened to your hair?

00:37:30.700 --> 00:37:33.060
Ah, you know, I felt like a...

00:37:34.300 --> 00:37:36.840
...n-new look, yeah?

00:37:37.710 --> 00:37:41.870
Jeez! Just because you didn't 
have time to do your hair!

00:37:42.300 --> 00:37:42.950
There!

00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:51.070
Listen up, Ren-san! We still have 
our whole lives ahead of us!

00:37:51.070 --> 00:37:52.650
Don't give up the fight!

00:37:52.650 --> 00:37:54.400
Uh, yeah...

00:37:55.430 --> 00:38:01.040
Now then! I'm going to work you girls ragged 
today—until your calluses are rough and hard!

00:38:01.040 --> 00:38:02.090
All right!

00:38:02.090 --> 00:38:05.440
Calluses...? Rough and hard...?

00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:10.100
All right, Yuina-chan, you'll 
start off cleaning the rooms.

00:38:10.100 --> 00:38:11.250
Here you go!

00:38:12.270 --> 00:38:14.870
The power's out already.

00:38:15.640 --> 00:38:17.980
Oh, right... That starts at nine.

00:38:17.980 --> 00:38:19.700
Way to remember, Yuina-san.

00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:22.890
And it's already ten past. Anyway,
I brought enough for everyone.

00:38:22.890 --> 00:38:25.570
Wow! Yuina-san, you're so thoughtful!

00:38:25.570 --> 00:38:29.740
That's because I've entered 
a new stage of development!

00:38:30.830 --> 00:38:31.730
I too am...

00:38:32.050 --> 00:38:33.640
I too am...

00:38:33.700 --> 00:38:35.860
...still developing in many areas!

00:38:36.900 --> 00:38:40.820
I may not look the part, 
but... Watch me go!

00:38:40.930 --> 00:38:41.730
Amazing!

00:38:41.730 --> 00:38:44.140
Tomoe-san's polishing the 
floor! What a rare sight!

00:38:45.910 --> 00:38:47.140
They've already started, huh...?

00:38:47.660 --> 00:38:50.750
All right, let's just do as much as 
we can with things as they are....

00:38:50.750 --> 00:38:52.210
I've finished prepping food for the staff!

00:38:52.210 --> 00:38:53.350
Right.

00:38:53.350 --> 00:38:55.350
We can't take a long lunch.

00:38:55.970 --> 00:38:57.480
Let's just eat it here.

00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:58.440
Yeah.

00:38:58.440 --> 00:39:00.690
Y-Yes, sir! I'll grab it at once!

00:39:01.090 --> 00:39:04.590
Should we alert our wholesaler then?

00:39:04.590 --> 00:39:05.780
Yeah.

00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:09.200
- <i>I worked on this all night long.</i>
- The power's out, so let's tell them soon.

00:39:09.200 --> 00:39:10.530
- <i>Tohru-san will definitely...</i>
- Understood.

00:39:10.530 --> 00:39:11.740
If that's the case...

00:39:11.740 --> 00:39:13.160
I've finished preparing it.

00:39:13.160 --> 00:39:13.950
Oh?

00:39:14.340 --> 00:39:16.890
Well, look at this. Quite elaborate...

00:39:16.890 --> 00:39:18.240
How do you eat it?

00:39:18.240 --> 00:39:21.500
Ah, you put whatever you want
on this baguette and eat—

00:39:21.500 --> 00:39:22.380
No good.

00:39:22.990 --> 00:39:23.920
Ren-san...

00:39:24.590 --> 00:39:28.490
Since we still have all the food prep
to do, I'll just go call them now.

00:39:28.490 --> 00:39:29.760
Okay, but what about this?

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:30.730
I'll eat it later.

00:39:39.180 --> 00:39:41.140
When you're done, please 
do the Paulownia Room.

00:39:41.140 --> 00:39:42.570
Aye-aye, sir!

00:39:46.460 --> 00:39:49.200
Yes, certainly. This area is...

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:51.620
Heave-ho!

00:39:51.620 --> 00:39:55.070
- Yuina-chan, come help me over here.
- Okie dokie!

00:39:57.100 --> 00:39:59.150
<i>Well, they seem to be getting along.</i>

00:40:08.330 --> 00:40:09.910
All right, all done.

00:40:11.100 --> 00:40:16.070
Yuina-san's festing it up, so we 
might be able to finish on time.

00:40:17.150 --> 00:40:22.150
That's a relief. I was worried, since 
we didn't have electricity...

00:40:22.150 --> 00:40:24.450
I still need to prepare for 
the field trip tomorrow...

00:40:24.450 --> 00:40:27.580
So I was hoping to get home early.

00:40:27.580 --> 00:40:29.430
Oh, you can just leave now.

00:40:29.740 --> 00:40:32.020
I'll finish up the rest for you.

00:40:32.020 --> 00:40:34.080
Huh? I couldn't do that to you.

00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:36.700
Don't worry! It's just one day.

00:40:36.700 --> 00:40:39.040
And the power outage is
over, anyway, right?

00:40:45.420 --> 00:40:46.210
Huh?

00:40:49.230 --> 00:40:50.590
WHAAAAAT!?

00:40:50.590 --> 00:40:52.760
I'm veeeery sorry!

00:40:53.330 --> 00:40:56.350
We completed the electrical
maintenance for the whole area,

00:40:56.350 --> 00:41:00.140
but a construction vehicle had an accident
 that left the area around Kissuiso...

00:41:00.140 --> 00:41:01.690
An accident?

00:41:02.100 --> 00:41:07.100
We'll keep working quickly, but I believe 
it will still take a bit longer to be fixed...

00:41:07.100 --> 00:41:08.860
You can't just say that...

00:41:08.860 --> 00:41:10.320
There's nothing we can do.

00:41:10.860 --> 00:41:13.220
These things can only be 
decided by God's will.

00:41:13.670 --> 00:41:14.570
Mother!

00:41:14.570 --> 00:41:15.480
Madam Manager.

00:41:16.350 --> 00:41:18.700
For what purpose do you 
have that brain of yours?

00:41:18.700 --> 00:41:22.370
Put your heads together, and 
decide the best course of action.

00:41:22.370 --> 00:41:23.860
Ren-san, how's the kitchen?

00:41:24.580 --> 00:41:29.510
Ma'am. We were planning to broil food,
but if we can't use the oven...

00:41:29.510 --> 00:41:31.950
We should switch to grilled 
food using charcoal fire.

00:41:31.950 --> 00:41:34.430
If we can't use the fridge...

00:41:34.430 --> 00:41:36.800
...the jellied fall vegetables 
will also be impossible.

00:41:37.190 --> 00:41:39.110
Maybe we can just lightly simmer them.

00:41:39.110 --> 00:41:41.860
- Tomoe, please inform our guests. 
- Nakochi, shouldn't you go?

00:41:41.860 --> 00:41:43.220
- There's no way.
- Understood!

00:41:43.220 --> 00:41:46.220
- I can't just go home the way things are.
- Denroku, prepare the emergency generators.

00:41:46.220 --> 00:41:47.770
I'll have to fest it up myself.

00:41:50.780 --> 00:41:52.970
Ah! Excuse me!

00:41:52.970 --> 00:41:54.360
H-Hello?

00:41:55.200 --> 00:41:57.190
Jeez, what is it, Tomoya?

00:41:57.190 --> 00:41:59.840
I told you to only call me 
if there's an emergency.

00:41:59.840 --> 00:42:03.500
<i>But... But it </i>is<i> an emergency...</i>

00:42:04.740 --> 00:42:06.050
Mana did what!?

00:42:06.050 --> 00:42:07.130
Nakochi?

00:42:07.570 --> 00:42:12.780
I-I was trying to help her get 
ready for the trip tomorrow,

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:14.330
but she started arguing with me...

00:42:14.670 --> 00:42:16.690
<i>Wait! When was this?</i>

00:42:16.690 --> 00:42:21.330
About th-thirty minutes ago. 
I looked for her, but...

00:42:21.810 --> 00:42:22.990
Enishing?

00:42:22.990 --> 00:42:24.310
Ah, Nako-chan!

00:42:24.310 --> 00:42:25.270
Nako!

00:42:25.270 --> 00:42:26.800
Nakochi, wait up!

00:42:27.950 --> 00:42:31.150
Having one or two of you missing 
won't change things here.

00:42:31.660 --> 00:42:33.110
Go with her.

00:42:34.690 --> 00:42:35.660
Okay!

00:42:38.930 --> 00:42:40.910
- Madam Manager, this isn't... 
- All right, everyone.

00:42:40.910 --> 00:42:42.540
You all know your jobs.

00:42:43.710 --> 00:42:46.890
We have to show we can 
overcome this. All right?

00:42:46.890 --> 00:42:48.790
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:42:51.390 --> 00:42:52.500
Mana!

00:42:52.730 --> 00:42:54.140
- Mana!
- Mana-chan!

00:42:59.370 --> 00:43:01.010
Mana!

00:43:01.830 --> 00:43:03.660
Mana!

00:43:04.140 --> 00:43:05.600
Mana-chan!

00:43:08.170 --> 00:43:09.400
Nakochi!

00:43:11.210 --> 00:43:15.310
It's no use. I was sure 
she'd be here, but...

00:43:15.310 --> 00:43:18.860
Let's keep looking. Is there 
anywhere else she'd be?

00:43:22.780 --> 00:43:23.770
Hello!?

00:43:23.770 --> 00:43:25.010
Mom?

00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:29.570
What? You called the police...!?

00:43:29.890 --> 00:43:31.960
It doesn't matter if you aren't here!

00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:34.980
I'll find Mana, no matter what!

00:43:34.980 --> 00:43:37.860
After I do, please go on 
her field trip with her...

00:43:38.220 --> 00:43:40.810
Who cares about your job!?

00:43:41.340 --> 00:43:42.560
Just come home!

00:43:42.560 --> 00:43:44.220
N-Nakochi...

00:43:44.220 --> 00:43:47.310
I never ever act selfish!

00:43:47.660 --> 00:43:49.390
I never do!

00:43:49.390 --> 00:43:50.570
Huh...?

00:43:50.570 --> 00:43:52.770
Can't you listen to me just this once!?

00:43:52.770 --> 00:43:58.050
I've always held it in. Just let me... 
For once, let <i>me</i> be selfish...!

00:43:59.190 --> 00:44:00.770
Just come home, please...!

00:44:04.460 --> 00:44:05.860
Nakochi...

00:44:05.860 --> 00:44:07.190
I held it in!

00:44:08.430 --> 00:44:12.100
That's right... I've always held things in.

00:44:12.510 --> 00:44:17.550
Even when you went out late at night and
it was dark, and I was afraid to be alone,

00:44:17.760 --> 00:44:19.460
I hate you, Mom

00:44:17.760 --> 00:44:19.470
I still didn't complain!

00:44:20.130 --> 00:44:22.840
Parents' Day at school, the zoo, the pool...

00:44:22.840 --> 00:44:26.310
I never complained when you let me down...

00:44:26.680 --> 00:44:29.310
You always told me you had to work.

00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:30.860
Even the other day!

00:44:30.860 --> 00:44:34.460
You promised Mana you'd go see
the show on that store's roof!

00:44:34.460 --> 00:44:36.380
And you broke that promise!

00:44:40.020 --> 00:44:43.400
She was really looking forward to it...

00:44:44.850 --> 00:44:46.100
Let's go!

00:44:46.100 --> 00:44:47.250
Huh?

00:44:48.220 --> 00:44:49.790
I think I know where Mana is.

00:45:08.510 --> 00:45:10.860
I've had something like this
happen to me before too...

00:45:11.860 --> 00:45:15.860
Mom broke her promise 
to take me to the zoo...

00:45:22.660 --> 00:45:24.310
I didn't want to give up.

00:45:24.310 --> 00:45:26.250
But since I didn't know 
how to get there...

00:45:26.660 --> 00:45:29.560
I went to a pet shop instead.

00:46:11.450 --> 00:46:12.620
Mana!

00:46:13.860 --> 00:46:14.800
Na...

00:46:16.250 --> 00:46:17.510
N-Na...

00:46:23.870 --> 00:46:24.890
Idiot...

00:46:25.430 --> 00:46:26.870
Mana you idiot!

00:46:26.870 --> 00:46:29.400
Why'd you run off like that!?

00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:33.790
B-But... But...

00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:36.350
Stupid! Aren't you going on
a field trip tomorrow!?

00:46:36.350 --> 00:46:37.880
- What if s—
- I don't wanna go!

00:46:41.240 --> 00:46:42.550
If Mommy...

00:46:43.340 --> 00:46:46.030
If Mommy...can't come...

00:46:46.620 --> 00:46:50.850
...then I don't wanna go on the trip!

00:46:50.850 --> 00:46:54.580
Everyone else will have their mommy.

00:46:54.580 --> 00:46:56.350
I don't wanna go!

00:47:07.810 --> 00:47:09.660
But won't I be with you?

00:47:10.430 --> 00:47:12.560
I'll go on the trip with you.

00:47:12.890 --> 00:47:15.350
And I'll make you a big lunch...

00:47:19.540 --> 00:47:20.900
So it's all right...

00:47:21.700 --> 00:47:22.740
Right?

00:47:30.140 --> 00:47:32.420
Wh-What's wrong, Ohana-chan?

00:47:32.750 --> 00:47:35.020
I-I don't know...

00:47:36.100 --> 00:47:40.090
I'm crying because you're not crying.

00:47:40.390 --> 00:47:46.340
You're still a kid, Nakochi, 
but you're acting like an adult...

00:47:46.340 --> 00:47:49.470
...even though you probably want to cry too.

00:47:49.470 --> 00:47:51.990
You're so amazing...

00:47:51.990 --> 00:47:54.430
You're totally pulling it off!

00:48:03.620 --> 00:48:06.210
Ohana-chan, you're...

00:48:21.350 --> 00:48:23.740
I called Tomoya, so he won't worry.

00:48:23.740 --> 00:48:25.630
Did he say sorry?

00:48:25.630 --> 00:48:29.350
Yeah, but you gotta say 
you're sorry too, okay?

00:48:29.350 --> 00:48:30.750
Okay!

00:48:35.570 --> 00:48:36.950
Bonbori...!?

00:48:45.300 --> 00:48:47.770
Wow, pretty!

00:48:48.470 --> 00:48:50.830
These are all...candles!

00:48:50.830 --> 00:48:53.120
Oh! You're back!

00:48:53.380 --> 00:48:56.120
Your sister's with you? 
That's a relief!

00:48:56.120 --> 00:48:59.080
Ah, um, what is...?

00:48:59.550 --> 00:49:03.220
We decided to turn the power outage 
into a CANDLE NIGHT! Isn't it great?

00:49:03.220 --> 00:49:04.300
I see...!

00:49:04.300 --> 00:49:07.390
I'm gonna put some more out over there!

00:49:07.990 --> 00:49:10.630
She's the one who thought of it.

00:49:10.630 --> 00:49:12.600
Huh, Yuina-san did!?

00:49:12.600 --> 00:49:15.560
The guests are really happy with it.

00:49:15.560 --> 00:49:18.900
Ren-san and the others 
worked hard on the food,

00:49:18.900 --> 00:49:21.480
but it seems like people were 
more excited for the outage.

00:49:21.480 --> 00:49:23.540
Over there, next!

00:49:23.540 --> 00:49:24.300
Let's go.

00:49:24.300 --> 00:49:25.380
Yeah!

00:49:26.780 --> 00:49:29.170
Such a horrifying child...

00:49:29.170 --> 00:49:32.010
That girl must have the 
God of Attendants with her!

00:49:32.010 --> 00:49:34.500
G-God of Attendants?

00:49:36.260 --> 00:49:39.250
I'm sorry for causing 
you so much trouble!

00:49:40.660 --> 00:49:43.420
Why didn't you just tell me earlier?

00:49:43.420 --> 00:49:44.330
Huh?

00:49:44.330 --> 00:49:48.170
If your parents are away, you needn't
 force yourself to come to work.

00:49:48.170 --> 00:49:52.340
B-But the power outage... And 
everyone was working so hard...

00:49:53.650 --> 00:49:57.930
What's the point of hiding it if you just
end up causing more trouble anyway?

00:49:57.930 --> 00:49:59.940
- Don't be mean to Nako!
- Mana-chan!

00:50:00.100 --> 00:50:01.060
M-Mana!

00:50:01.060 --> 00:50:01.820
Mana-chan!

00:50:01.820 --> 00:50:03.180
Hey, Mana...

00:50:03.180 --> 00:50:04.810
- Let go! 
- Hey!

00:50:04.810 --> 00:50:07.250
Why don't you take her 
with you to the bath?

00:50:13.150 --> 00:50:14.780
Towel jellyfish!

00:50:14.780 --> 00:50:16.740
Wow, amazing!

00:50:16.740 --> 00:50:18.090
I'm heading out.

00:50:18.090 --> 00:50:19.620
See you later!

00:50:23.150 --> 00:50:26.110
The water feels good...

00:50:26.110 --> 00:50:27.430
I'm beat...

00:50:27.430 --> 00:50:29.910
I'm sorry if I troubled you.

00:50:29.910 --> 00:50:31.510
Ah, no, it has nothing to do with y—

00:50:31.510 --> 00:50:32.640
Splash!

00:50:33.580 --> 00:50:34.770
Splashy!

00:50:34.770 --> 00:50:37.500
Hey, Mana! The bath isn't a place to play.

00:50:37.500 --> 00:50:39.510
Wait! I wanna swim, too!

00:50:43.390 --> 00:50:45.390
That's quite a ruckus in there...

00:50:48.650 --> 00:50:50.300
Mom!

00:50:50.300 --> 00:50:53.030
- Satsuki got out without counting to 100!
- Shut up!

00:50:53.030 --> 00:50:54.610
Enishi, you chimpanzee!

00:51:04.730 --> 00:51:06.460
I'm a ghost!

00:51:06.460 --> 00:51:08.080
Ghost! Ghost!

00:51:08.630 --> 00:51:11.550
Come on, Mana. Make sure 
you wear your undies.

00:51:11.550 --> 00:51:17.480
Wow! So cool! I wanna do it 
too! Lemme try, lemme try!

00:51:17.480 --> 00:51:18.720
- Okay. 
- Mana!

00:51:19.050 --> 00:51:20.660
I got a text message from Mom!

00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:22.140
She said she can go on the field trip!

00:51:22.140 --> 00:51:23.270
What, really?

00:51:23.270 --> 00:51:24.110
Yeah!

00:51:24.740 --> 00:51:27.760
Yay! Yaaay!

00:51:28.280 --> 00:51:30.700
Ah hey, put your undies o—

00:51:31.780 --> 00:51:33.980
But Nako, you gotta make lunch, okay!?

00:51:33.980 --> 00:51:36.510
Like the huge one you do
for New Year's, okay?

00:51:36.860 --> 00:51:40.850
For New Year's? It's too 
late to start that now.

00:51:40.850 --> 00:51:45.110
- Aww, but Mana wants a big lunch!
- I'm happy for her.

00:51:45.110 --> 00:51:45.930
Yeah.

00:51:58.390 --> 00:52:00.420
I should put this back.

00:52:04.300 --> 00:52:07.970
I guess...there's nothing 
more about Mom in here...

00:52:09.030 --> 00:52:10.360
That makes sense.

00:52:10.670 --> 00:52:13.130
She'd already be in Tokyo by this time.

00:52:14.050 --> 00:52:17.910
<i>All the things about Mom 
not written here...</i>

00:52:18.820 --> 00:52:22.500
<i>She wasn't an adult from the start either.</i>

00:52:22.500 --> 00:52:27.420
<i>At first, she probably didn't know how to 
sparkle, or really understand being in love.</i>

00:52:27.750 --> 00:52:33.870
<i>It was gradual, through having emotional 
experiences. And so, little by little...</i>

00:52:34.450 --> 00:52:35.130
Huh?

00:52:35.130 --> 00:52:37.380
Satsuki-chan returns. And a small guest. 
Her daughter, Ohana-chan. So lovely.

00:52:37.380 --> 00:52:38.700
"Ohana"?

00:52:40.080 --> 00:52:41.550
Me...?

00:52:55.310 --> 00:52:56.880
Phew.

00:52:57.960 --> 00:52:59.410
Right!

00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:04.490
The lights are back on...

00:53:07.220 --> 00:53:07.780
Huh?

00:53:08.170 --> 00:53:09.310
Minchi?

00:53:09.570 --> 00:53:11.730
Wh-What are you doing, barging in!?

00:53:11.730 --> 00:53:13.060
S-Sorry...

00:53:13.060 --> 00:53:16.340
I thought I'd try making a
monster lunch for Mana.

00:53:18.710 --> 00:53:21.300
Minchi, were you thinking the same thing?

00:53:21.960 --> 00:53:26.560
W-Well, I just figured making this kind 
of stuff would be good practice...

00:53:26.560 --> 00:53:27.580
That's all!

00:53:27.580 --> 00:53:28.220
I see...

00:53:32.420 --> 00:53:36.090
U-Um... What is...that?

00:53:36.690 --> 00:53:38.760
Ah, is it a Hokémon!?

00:53:38.760 --> 00:53:39.690
No!

00:53:40.370 --> 00:53:41.380
B-Booty Cure...

00:53:41.380 --> 00:53:43.370
Huh? That's a person?

00:53:44.030 --> 00:53:47.770
Y-You really are a...

00:53:49.020 --> 00:53:50.170
HOT VIT LON!

00:53:51.180 --> 00:53:53.930
Sorry, sorry! Hey, it looks totally fine!

00:53:53.930 --> 00:53:58.570
These chicken nuggets are cute and 
tiny, just the right size for Mana!

00:53:59.660 --> 00:54:02.390
And it's nice and colorful, 
with the red and yellow...

00:54:02.390 --> 00:54:05.930
Th-That's why! Since the skin 
is made with egg strips,

00:54:05.930 --> 00:54:08.300
I didn't think it was a person!

00:54:08.300 --> 00:54:08.900
Booty Cure!

00:54:08.900 --> 00:54:10.170
Just drop that!

00:54:11.660 --> 00:54:15.140
But you sure put a lot of thought 
into making the food for Mana.

00:54:15.140 --> 00:54:16.510
Well, yeah...

00:54:16.940 --> 00:54:20.190
As a chef, one has to 
consider the customer...

00:54:22.990 --> 00:54:27.140
<i>Back then, the flavor was too strong
to serve to the older guests.</i>

00:54:28.670 --> 00:54:29.770
<i>And then that time...</i>

00:54:30.350 --> 00:54:34.040
<i>I made a very complicated meal, 
even though we were all busy.</i>

00:54:36.050 --> 00:54:38.010
<i>I wasn't considering at all...</i>

00:54:38.670 --> 00:54:41.050
<i>...the individuals who would eat the meals...</i>

00:54:41.730 --> 00:54:44.820
Heeeey, Minchi?

00:54:44.820 --> 00:54:46.170
Heeeey!

00:54:47.690 --> 00:54:51.930
Once we finish this lunch box, you're 
helping me think up a new menu!

00:54:52.940 --> 00:54:54.820
Huuuuh, why me!?

00:54:54.820 --> 00:54:57.710
- I can't tell if they get along or not...
- 'Cause it's you! You have time to, right!?

00:54:58.690 --> 00:55:00.430
Huh? What's this?

00:55:00.430 --> 00:55:02.010
Shut up! Hot vit lon!

00:55:02.010 --> 00:55:03.860
What? That's the second time!

00:55:03.860 --> 00:55:05.770
My next work will be...

00:55:05.770 --> 00:55:09.260
"Newbie Chef's Midnight Mushroom Soup"!

00:55:09.260 --> 00:55:11.560
Or something... Maybe?

00:55:24.220 --> 00:55:29.720
Routine maintenance, construction vehicle
accident. Everyone fested it up.

00:55:36.010 --> 00:55:40.510
Now what should I do?

00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:57.140
J-Just a little longer, Ohana...

00:55:59.130 --> 00:56:00.590
That smell!

00:56:03.230 --> 00:56:06.460
Gross... It's all slimy.

00:56:06.460 --> 00:56:08.500
What <i>was</i> this anyway?

00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:13.110
This sort of thing really 
sucks without Ohana.

00:56:14.060 --> 00:56:16.510
Guess I gotta suck it up and take 
out the trash this morning.

00:56:18.930 --> 00:56:20.820
Yeah, yeah, yeah...

00:56:23.770 --> 00:56:25.590
This is Matsumae.

00:56:25.590 --> 00:56:27.100
Ah, brother-in-law!?

00:56:27.460 --> 00:56:29.130
It's been a long time!

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:33.780
Yeah, I'm doing fine... 
Ohana, too.

00:56:34.750 --> 00:56:36.580
Oh, that's right.

00:56:36.580 --> 00:56:40.070
We managed to find a sponsor; 
now we can hold a photo exhibit.

00:56:41.110 --> 00:56:46.130
Yeah, even now, some people 
are still fond of his pictures.

00:56:47.220 --> 00:56:48.320
Yeah, that's right.

00:56:49.130 --> 00:56:52.610
Since we have this opportunity, I thought we 
could use some of his personal photos, too.

00:56:52.610 --> 00:56:57.010
So I was wondering if there were
any of his photos left at your place...

00:56:58.950 --> 00:57:00.820
I'm thinking "Ohana" for the name.

00:57:02.500 --> 00:57:04.100
Ohana?

00:57:04.100 --> 00:57:07.830
So that she can grow beautifully 
like a flower or something?

00:57:07.830 --> 00:57:09.870
Yeah, but...

00:57:10.330 --> 00:57:12.260
It's also a Hawaiian word...

00:57:12.260 --> 00:57:14.080
It means family.

00:57:14.660 --> 00:57:15.710
"Ohana."

00:57:17.020 --> 00:57:18.330
Family...

00:57:18.540 --> 00:57:20.560
Yeah, family.

00:57:21.740 --> 00:57:23.190
Family, huh...?

00:57:24.010 --> 00:57:26.250
Yeah, I think I like it.

00:57:26.670 --> 00:57:28.110
Are you ready?

00:57:35.490 --> 00:57:37.590
Further! Further!

00:57:37.590 --> 00:57:39.310
Further! Further!

00:57:39.310 --> 00:57:41.950
Sorry, but I'm going to 
have to call you back!

00:57:41.950 --> 00:57:44.100
Yeah, thanks for that.

00:57:44.650 --> 00:57:46.970
Crap, can I still make it?

00:57:53.780 --> 00:57:55.790
Guess there's no choice. Time to run!

00:57:56.050 --> 00:57:58.160
Ack, we overslept!

00:57:58.940 --> 00:58:00.770
Minchi, we gotta hurry!

00:58:01.620 --> 00:58:03.170
Hey, Ohana!

00:58:03.170 --> 00:58:06.110
Wait! Running will ruin the lunch 
we worked so hard on!

00:58:06.350 --> 00:58:08.140
But we aren't going to make it!

00:58:08.140 --> 00:58:09.050
Just run straight!

00:58:09.050 --> 00:58:11.930
- What in the world is this ruckus...?
- Okay, got it!

00:58:14.060 --> 00:58:16.380
The weather's lovely this morning.

00:58:19.140 --> 00:58:20.270
The train?

00:58:20.270 --> 00:58:22.510
We can't... The next one's 
coming in 30 minutes!

00:58:22.510 --> 00:58:24.810
We're not gonna make it for the field trip!

00:58:25.330 --> 00:58:26.700
Minchi, wait up!

00:58:26.700 --> 00:58:28.270
There's no time!

00:58:30.830 --> 00:58:32.470
You're late!

00:58:32.470 --> 00:58:35.340
- If we don't hurry, we'll be late! Hurry up! 
- Sorry...

00:58:35.340 --> 00:58:37.780
<i>Seriously, it's so out of the blue!</i>

00:58:37.780 --> 00:58:39.930
<i>Are you planning to stay back
 at home permanently?</i>

00:58:39.930 --> 00:58:42.540
I still haven't even talked with my mother.

00:58:42.540 --> 00:58:46.450
I'm not sure how things will go, 
but I'll figure something out.

00:58:46.450 --> 00:58:50.750
<i>It really is unfortunate about your
husband, but this sure is a waste.</i>

00:58:50.750 --> 00:58:54.500
<i>Just as you finally got on track
as a writer and everything...</i>

00:58:55.330 --> 00:58:56.340
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:58:56.340 --> 00:58:59.810
S-Sorry... I'll call you back 
when things calm down.

00:58:59.810 --> 00:59:01.180
Good-bye.

00:59:08.140 --> 00:59:09.580
Shush, shush...

00:59:09.580 --> 00:59:11.780
Such a cute baby!

00:59:11.780 --> 00:59:14.240
Totally! She's so tiny!

00:59:16.770 --> 00:59:17.870
Guess I should go.

00:59:35.050 --> 00:59:37.340
Long time no see, Beans.

00:59:37.340 --> 00:59:39.310
Satsuki-chan...

00:59:40.180 --> 00:59:41.770
Is that your...?

00:59:43.050 --> 00:59:44.740
Her name is Ohana.

00:59:46.270 --> 00:59:47.610
Natural curls.

00:59:48.630 --> 00:59:51.860
Our family's always had 
stiff, straight hair...

00:59:51.860 --> 00:59:53.910
This is probably from her father.

00:59:58.170 --> 01:00:00.330
She's very...lovely.

01:00:00.860 --> 01:00:01.940
Thanks.

01:00:03.300 --> 01:00:05.820
Hey, do you know where Mom is?

01:00:05.820 --> 01:00:07.120
Madam Manager is...

01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:08.470
I am terribly sorry!

01:00:09.780 --> 01:00:11.120
It's all right, Ren...

01:00:11.120 --> 01:00:11.990
I'm terribly sorry!

01:00:12.330 --> 01:00:13.740
I'm terribly sorry!

01:00:13.740 --> 01:00:16.870
I-It's all because I messed up the order.

01:00:17.660 --> 01:00:20.380
With the stormy weather, we 
haven't had a good catch...

01:00:20.380 --> 01:00:24.350
Madam Manager, everyone's really busy,
so they aren't able to help...

01:00:24.940 --> 01:00:26.380
I'll take responsibility!

01:00:26.380 --> 01:00:27.310
I will qui—

01:00:27.310 --> 01:00:30.020
If you quitting would 
solve this problem,

01:00:30.020 --> 01:00:32.360
I'd happily let you do so.

01:00:32.730 --> 01:00:35.300
But this is no longer only your problem.

01:00:35.300 --> 01:00:37.320
This is Kissuiso's problem.

01:00:37.660 --> 01:00:42.100
Kissuiso is everyone's inn. Understand?

01:00:42.420 --> 01:00:44.940
We will get through this together.

01:00:44.940 --> 01:00:46.540
Y-Yes, ma'am!

01:00:46.540 --> 01:00:49.470
Renji, there are plenty of 
things you could be doing.

01:00:49.470 --> 01:00:51.180
Yes, ma'am! I'm sorry!

01:00:51.900 --> 01:00:52.860
<i>Mom...</i>

01:00:53.980 --> 01:00:56.110
<i>Back then, I didn't understand a thing.</i>

01:00:56.430 --> 01:01:00.500
- Don't just stand around like that. 
- <i>Mom wasn't clinging onto Dad's ghost.</i>

01:01:01.550 --> 01:01:03.930
<i>And she wasn't clinging to the past.</i>

01:01:03.930 --> 01:01:05.370
<i>Mom can't...</i>

01:01:06.660 --> 01:01:08.180
She can't lose...

01:01:08.460 --> 01:01:12.610
- If you need more vegetables, ask Fukuya. 
- <i>She probably can't bear to lose...</i>

01:01:13.850 --> 01:01:19.240
<i>She can't lose to herself... So that 
she can look toward the future...</i>

01:01:23.340 --> 01:01:25.260
S-Satsuki-cha—

01:01:25.260 --> 01:01:27.940
Don't tell Mom I was here, okay?

01:01:31.260 --> 01:01:32.750
Take care, Beans.

01:01:44.300 --> 01:01:47.010
Like I'd lose to you, stupid bitch.

01:01:58.830 --> 01:02:00.080
Having fun?

01:02:00.480 --> 01:02:04.540
Yeah! We gotta live life to the fullest!

01:02:04.890 --> 01:02:06.980
Isn't that right, Ohana?

01:02:08.210 --> 01:02:09.210
Let's go.

01:02:09.410 --> 01:02:15.340
Every single time that our eyes met,
I could feel my cheeks begin to blush

01:02:09.410 --> 01:02:15.340
<i>kimi to me ga au tabi akaku somaru hoho wo</i>

01:02:15.340 --> 01:02:21.760
so I blamed it all on the orange
sun that was just about to set

01:02:15.340 --> 01:02:21.760
<i>shizumikaketa orenji no sei ni shita</i>

01:02:21.760 --> 01:02:27.760
The dream-like feelings that I have now,
I wish I could lock them in their place

01:02:21.760 --> 01:02:27.760
<i>yume no youna ima wo sukoshi mo iroasezu ni</i>

01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:35.440
inside my heart so that
they will never fade away

01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:35.440
<i>kokoro ni shimatte oketara iina</i>

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:38.530
Wait, I have trash!

01:02:56.450 --> 01:02:58.220
Nakochi!

01:03:11.740 --> 01:03:16.980
Two shadows stretch out far
away and become so very long

01:03:11.740 --> 01:03:16.980
<i>hosoku nagaku nobita futatsu no kage</i>

01:03:16.980 --> 01:03:22.070
They perfectly depict the 
light touch of twilight

01:03:16.980 --> 01:03:22.070
<i>marude e ni egaita youna yuugure ni</i>

01:03:22.650 --> 01:03:27.740
Our voices full of mirth 
and so loudly echoing,

01:03:22.650 --> 01:03:27.740
<i>okashi na pohzu wo utsusu kaerimichi</i>

01:03:27.740 --> 01:03:33.500
as we make strange 
poses on the way home...

01:03:27.740 --> 01:03:33.500
<i>waraigoe kodama suru</i>

01:03:44.820 --> 01:03:50.010
Two shadows stretch out far
away and become so very long

01:03:44.820 --> 01:03:50.010
<i>hosoku nagaku nobita futatsu no kage</i>

01:03:50.010 --> 01:03:55.780
Their two hands held together 
might seem embarrassing

01:03:50.010 --> 01:03:55.780
<i>kasanatta te to te ga terekusakute</i>

01:03:55.780 --> 01:04:06.210
We'll lose if we tread on top of our shadow, 
so I use that as an excuse to run!

01:03:55.780 --> 01:04:06.210
<i>kage wo fumaretara makedanante 
iiwake ni hashiridasu</i>

01:04:06.210 --> 01:04:11.870
Every single time that our eyes met,
I could feel my cheeks begin to blush

01:04:06.210 --> 01:04:11.870
<i>kimi to me ga au tabi akaku somaru hoho wo</i>

01:04:11.870 --> 01:04:17.400
so I blamed it all on the orange 
sun that was just about to set

01:04:11.870 --> 01:04:17.400
<i>shizumikaketa orenji no sei ni shita</i>

01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:22.840
The dream-like feelings that I have now,
I wish I could lock them in their place

01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:22.840
<i>yume no youna ima wo sukoshi mo iroasezu ni</i>

01:04:22.840 --> 01:04:28.890
inside my heart so that
they will never fade away

01:04:22.840 --> 01:04:28.890
<i>kokoro ni shimatte oketara iina</i>

01:04:50.350 --> 01:04:55.950
The flower-like sunset lent its colors 
and dyed the whole world,

01:04:50.350 --> 01:04:55.950
<i>hana no youna yuuyake wa sekai wo somete</i>

01:04:55.950 --> 01:05:01.450
marking the slow flow of time
 as it continues to march on

01:04:55.950 --> 01:05:01.450
<i>nagaretsuzukeru jikan ni shirushi wo tsuketa</i>

01:05:01.450 --> 01:05:07.220
And when a laugh happened to part your
lips, I just couldn't take my eyes away

01:05:01.450 --> 01:05:07.220
<i>ichibyougoto ni kawariyuku kokoro dakara</i>

01:05:07.220 --> 01:05:12.600
because feelings change constantly; 
a new one every second

01:05:07.220 --> 01:05:12.600
<i>kimi ga warau shunkan wo minogasanuyouni</i>

01:05:12.600 --> 01:05:18.100
Our stretched out shadows 
and my blushing cheeks

01:05:12.600 --> 01:05:18.100
<i>nagaku nobita kage mo akaku somaru hoho mo</i>

01:05:18.100 --> 01:05:23.600
the warmth when we 
held hands and the grip

01:05:18.100 --> 01:05:23.600
<i>tsunaida te no ondo mo sono chikara mo</i>

01:05:23.600 --> 01:05:28.940
Everything that we have right here,
 I wish I could lock it into place

01:05:23.600 --> 01:05:28.940
<i>ima koko ni aru subete wo sukoshi mo iroasezu ni</i>

01:05:28.940 --> 01:05:34.700
inside my heart so that
it will never fade away

01:05:28.940 --> 01:05:34.700
<i>kokoro ni shimatte oketara iina</i>

01:05:34.700 --> 01:05:40.160
And I want the opportunity to
 be the one to stomp through

01:05:34.700 --> 01:05:40.160
<i>kimi no kokoro ni sumu kage wo hitotsu hitotsu</i>

01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:45.660
every shadow that resides anywhere
within your sweet heart

01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:45.660
<i>kono ashi de fumitsukete yukitaikara</i>

01:05:45.660 --> 01:05:51.090
Even as the seasons change,
 as they always will do

01:05:45.660 --> 01:05:51.090
<i>kisetsu ga mata megutte mo 
futatsu no kage wa zutto</i>

01:05:51.090 --> 01:05:57.780
I hope the two shadows 
will always be together

01:05:51.090 --> 01:05:57.780
<i>tonariatte irareretara iina</i>
